---
import EyebrowLabel from "../ui/EyebrowLabel.astro";
---

<section class="section" id="why">
  <div class="problem__inner">
    <EyebrowLabel>Why LoyaltyOS</EyebrowLabel>
    <h2 class="section-title problem__h2">
      Loyalty software shouldn't be a black box.
    </h2>
    <div class="problem__body">
      <p class="section-body">
        Most loyalty platforms lock your customer data behind opaque SaaS
        pricing, charge per active member, and treat coalition programs as a
        roadmap promise. When a campaign breaks at midnight on Black Friday, you
        file a ticket and wait.
      </p>
      <p class="section-body">
        LoyaltyOS flips that. Every points ledger entry lives in your Postgres.
        Every campaign rule lives in your repo. Every adapter — including the
        one for Puntos Apprecio — is open code you can read, fork, and extend.
        And every operation is exposed as an MCP tool, so your team can run the
        program from Claude, ChatGPT, or any agent they already use. Your
        loyalty program is infrastructure you own.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .problem__h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 792px;
  }

  .problem__body {
    max-width: 588px;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
